course: dictionary
lesson: 14151
title: Saying words right
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To mispronounce a word is to say it in the wrong way, with the wrong sounds or the wrong stress. Stress means which part of the word you push hardest. «I always mispronounce library, so my teacher said it again, slowly.»
explain: The start of the word, mis-, is a clue. It means wrong, as in misspell and misread. If you say a word wrongly, you have mispronounced it.
explain: Many people mispronounce words they have only ever read, because they have never heard them said out loud. When you meet a new word in a book, look it up in a dictionary to hear how it is said, or ask someone who knows.
fact: «Mispronounce» means to say a word or a name in the wrong way.
fact: «Mispronounce» is a verb: I mispronounce, she mispronounces, they mispronounced, we are mispronouncing.
fact: Stress is the part of a word you say most strongly, as in «PHO-to» and «pho-TOG-ra-phy».
fact: A commonly mispronounced word is one that many people say wrongly, such as «library», said lie-brer-ee, not lie-berry.
fact: It is kind to ask someone how to say their name, then say it the way they tell you.
exercise: «Tom kept saying lie-berry for library.» What has Tom done? | Spelled the word wrongly | *Mispronounced the word | Written a new word | Read the word aloud perfectly
exercise: Why is it kind to ask how someone says their name? | *Because people can easily mispronounce a name | Because you must write it down twice | Because names never change | Because names are always hard to spell
exercise: Which word means to say a word in the wrong way? | Copy | *Mispronounce | Whisper | Spell
test: «The actor kept mispronouncing the king's name, so the audience giggled.» What does mispronouncing mean here? | Writing the name in big letters | Forgetting the name on purpose | Singing the name loudly | *Saying the name in the wrong way
test: A commonly mispronounced word is one that many people say wrongly. Which word is often mispronounced in English lessons? | blue | *library | cat | run
exam: Which sentence uses mispronounce correctly? | *«Readers often mispronounce words they only know from books.» | «The bird mispronounced its song at dawn.» | «We mispronounced a nice cake for tea.»
